  ("Alignment of Paragraphs in Bilingual Texts" 0.4564 0.8233 0.0439 0.0564 0.0564 0.0125 0.0053 0.3204 0.0894)
  ("825" 0.8706 0.9022 0.0439 0.0564 0.0564 0.0125 nil 0.0000 0.0316)
  ("paper 8 we have suggested an alignment method based on measuring similarity using" 0.0981 0.9029 0.0870 0.1008 0.1008 0.0138 0.0068 0.2853 0.0519)
  ("bilingual dictionaries and presented an approximate heuristic greedy alignment algo-" 0.0981 0.9027 0.1045 0.1183 0.1183 0.0138 0.0076 0.2505 0.0824)
  ("rithm. In this paper our goals are:" 0.0981 0.4087 0.1219 0.1358 0.1358 0.0138 0.0059 0.3046 0.0557)
  ("–" 0.0981 0.1097 0.1485 0.1623 0.1623 0.0138 nil nil 0.0116)
  ("–" 0.0981 0.1097 0.1659 0.1798 0.1798 0.0138 nil nil 0.0116)
  ("–" 0.0981 0.1097 0.2007 0.2145 0.2145 0.0138 nil nil 0.0116)
  ("–" 0.0981 0.1097 0.2181 0.2319 0.2319 0.0138 nil nil 0.0116)
  ("To formalize the paragraph alignment task, casting it as an optimization problem;" 0.1400 0.8978 0.1485 0.1623 0.1623 0.0138 0.0059 0.3222 0.0261)
  ("To introduce an algorithm that finds the exact optimum of this problem, instead" 0.1400 0.9023 0.1659 0.1798 0.1798 0.0138 0.0076 0.2984 0.0261)
  ("of the approximate heuristic-based algorithm;" 0.1400 0.5647 0.1832 0.1970 0.1970 0.0138 0.0059 0.2957 0.0193)
  ("To suggest a distance measure for paragraphs that guarantees unbiased solution;" 0.1400 0.8849 0.2007 0.2145 0.2145 0.0138 0.0059 0.2525 0.0261)
  ("To propose a baseline distance measure and to compare the results obtained with" 0.1400 0.9024 0.2181 0.2319 0.2319 0.0138 0.0068 0.2673 0.0261)
  ("our suggested measure against such a baseline." 0.1397 0.5753 0.2356 0.2494 0.2494 0.0138 0.0059 0.2507 0.0308)
  ("The optimization problem resulting from our formalization of the task strongly re-" 0.1246 0.9028 0.2621 0.2759 0.2759 0.0138 0.0068 0.3057 0.0362)
  ("sembles string alignment problems, such as optimal string alignment or calculating" 0.0981 0.9026 0.2796 0.2934 0.2934 0.0138 0.0092 0.2875 0.0746)
  ("the Levenshtein distance between strings. Inspired in standard methods for solving" 0.0981 0.9025 0.2968 0.3107 0.3107 0.0138 0.0093 0.2298 0.0281)
  ("problems of this class, we developed a dynamic programming algorithm. However," 0.0981 0.9025 0.3143 0.3281 0.3281 0.0138 0.0088 0.2893 0.0862)
  ("our formalization differs from the optimal string alignment. That latter task requires" 0.0981 0.9024 0.3317 0.3456 0.3456 0.0138 0.0081 0.2963 0.0309)
  ("aligning some symbols in a string with at most one symbol in the other string; in our" 0.0981 0.9025 0.3492 0.3630 0.3630 0.0138 0.0071 0.3088 0.0761)
  ("case, we align every symbol with at least one symbol in the other string. This leads to" 0.0981 0.9025 0.3667 0.3805 0.3805 0.0138 0.0065 0.3076 0.0457)
  ("a modification of the algorithm." 0.0981 0.3944 0.3841 0.3979 0.3979 0.0138 0.0059 0.3391 0.0103)
  ("The paper is organized as follows. In Section 0, we explain the task in detail and" 0.1246 0.9026 0.4014 0.4152 0.4152 0.0138 0.0078 0.2483 0.0362)
  ("formalize it as an optimization problem. In Section 0, we introduce a baseline and a" 0.0981 0.9025 0.4188 0.4327 0.4327 0.0138 0.0079 0.2762 0.0889)
  ("suggested distance measures between paragraphs, which are used for calculation of" 0.0981 0.9025 0.4363 0.4501 0.4501 0.0138 0.0090 0.2173 0.0914)
  ("the cost function to be optimized. In Section 0, we present a dynamic programming" 0.0981 0.9025 0.4537 0.4676 0.4676 0.0138 0.0081 0.2813 0.0282)
  ("algorithm that finds the exact optimum of the problem. In Section 0, we discuss its" 0.0981 0.9026 0.4712 0.4850 0.4850 0.0138 0.0085 0.2908 0.0903)
  ("complexity. Finally, in Section 0 we present the experimental results and in Section 0" 0.0981 0.9023 0.4885 0.5023 0.5023 0.0138 0.0066 0.2937 0.1101)
  ("give conclusions and discuss the possible future work." 0.0981 0.6030 0.5059 0.5198 0.5198 0.0138 0.0060 0.2544 0.0396)
  ("2 Paragraph-Level Text Alignment" 0.0981 0.5296 0.5516 0.5680 0.5680 0.0164 0.0070 0.2933 0.0140)
  ("Given a text and its translation into another language, the text alignment task consists" 0.0981 0.9025 0.5898 0.6036 0.6036 0.0138 0.0067 0.2767 0.0568)
  ("in determining which text elements (such as words) are translations of each other, as" 0.0981 0.9024 0.6072 0.6210 0.6210 0.0138 0.0073 0.2740 0.0181)
  ("shown in Fig. 1, where words that are translations of each other are connected by" 0.0981 0.9028 0.6247 0.6385 0.6385 0.0138 0.0098 0.2261 0.0604)
  ("lines. In such simple cases the text alignment task can be formalized as building a" 0.0981 0.9024 0.6421 0.6559 0.6559 0.0138 0.0090 0.2455 0.0495)
  ("bipartite graph whose vertices are the text elements and an arc connects two vertices" 0.0981 0.9026 0.6594 0.6732 0.6732 0.0138 0.0074 0.2525 0.0776)
  ("if the corresponding elements are translations of each other." 0.0981 0.6539 0.6768 0.6907 0.6907 0.0138 0.0058 0.2684 0.0142)
